 "text": "During the Vietnam War, the US Army tried to scare enemy soldiers with ghosts. It was called Operation Wandering Soul. In Vietnamese tradition, if you die far from home without proper burial, your soul can wander forever. So the Army recorded eerie voices, dead soldiers begging their friends to go home, then played them from speakers at night. Here's the trick. Use what people already fear. It didn't always work. Sometimes they just shot at the speakers. Follow for more dark psychology.",
